[stderr] | Age rating, parental controls, regions, store/certification, and legal policy | requires-decision | Applicable requirements are named but audience detail, regions, and commerce/service scope are unknown. | Cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Scope and dependency conclusions
[stderr] 
[stderr] The minimal offline campaign depends on the shell, exploration, narrative,
[stderr] quests/progression, combat, inventory, persistence, rendering/input,
[stderr] accessibility, original assets, content tooling, and quality disciplines. PWA
[stderr] packaging adds installability, caches, offline assets, and update safety; it
[stderr] does not create a separate game.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Account, multiplayer, live-service, and commerce must not become dependencies
[stderr] of the offline campaign until a human resolves their contradiction. If approved,
[stderr] they require explicit degraded states, privacy/security rules, operational
[stderr] ownership, and recovery behavior. If deferred, their interfaces and data model
[stderr] must not expand or block the first release.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Explicit requests, safe assumptions, and approval gates
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Kind | Discovery conclusion | Handling |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Explicit requests | Small 2D single-player RPG; web/PWA; exploration, town, dungeon, combat, inventory, quests, saves, settings, ending, access, feedback, recovery. | Plan as the complete offline campaign. |
[stderr] | Necessary implied capabilities | Shell/session, authored content/tooling, input/rendering, QA, release/update workflow, and balance. | Include in later contracts as enabling work, sized to the small release. |
[stderr] | Safe assumptions | Original content; shared core; durable confirmed local saves when storage permits; connected features visibly degrade; minimal-data diagnostics. | Retain as reversible guardrails only. |
[stderr] | Approval gates | Connected scope, account/sync, multiplayer/safety, commerce, stack/vendors, support matrix/budgets, content quantities, localisation, audio, and legal/store policy. | Record and obtain approval before selecting policies, services, or production quantities. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Reference boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] The functional reference constrains high-level party-based turn-based adventure
[stderr] scope only. It is never permission to reproduce branding, names, copy, story,
[stderr] characters, lore, assets, music, layouts, screen composition, maps, distinctive
[stderr] menus, flows, or interaction choreography. Original mechanics expression,
[stderr] content, UI, art, and feedback must be created for this product.
[stderr] # 01 — Product brief
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Canonical normalized brief:** [`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md).
[stderr] `INITIAL.md` remains the source of truth. This specification intentionally adds
[stderr] no requirements or decisions beyond that document.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Release definition
[stderr] 
[stderr] Deliver an original, small, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG for a
[stderr] responsive public web application and installable PWA. The complete path is one
[stderr] town, one dungeon, onboarding, readable narrative/quests, tutorialized
[stderr] party-based turn-based combat, inventory/progression, save/load/recovery,
[stderr] settings/accessibility, and a short ending.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Requirement handling
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Direct requests define the candidate first-release scope and measurable
[stderr]   outcomes in the canonical brief.
[stderr] - Safe assumptions are temporary guardrails, not service, legal, technology,
[stderr]   content, or vendor commitments.
[stderr] - Deferred roadmap work is not release acceptance work.
[stderr] - Connected services and commerce remain unresolved because they conflict with
[stderr]   the stated offline single-player product; downstream contracts need human
[stderr]   approval before selecting their architecture or policy.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Originality boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] The named game is a functional scope reference only. No branding, copy, assets,
[stderr] layouts, interaction choreography, or other protected expression may be copied.
[stderr] All content, presentation, mechanics expression, and player interfaces must be
[stderr] independently designed.
[stderr] 
